            <ArticleTitle>Misery and myth: a connection between society and inadequate pain control?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>75-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite numerous studies and re-education strategies spanning two decades, inadequate relief of pain remains a significant problem for both clients and nurses. This paper explores the literature on the extent of the problem and suggests that societal attitudes about narcotic drugs are a major contributing factor to this problem. Encouraging reflective practice is one of the strategies suggested to address the situation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
